  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simple interest: interest and amount (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} deposits Ksh \( {@P0@} \) in a bank account that pays <strong>simple interest</strong> at \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum.</p>
<p>(a) How much interest will {@nm@} earn in \( {@T0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Interest \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) What will the total amount in the account be after \( {@T0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Amount \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> With \( P = {@P0@} \), \( R = {@R0@} \) and \( T = {@T0@} \):</p>
\[ I = \frac{P \times R \times T}{100} = \frac{ {@P0@} \times {@R0@} \times {@T0@} }{100} = {@si@}. \]
<p>The interest is Ksh \( {@si@} \). Each year the account earns the same Ksh \( {@si/T0@} \), because simple interest is always calculated on the original deposit.</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Amount \( = P + I = {@P0@} + {@si@} = \) Ksh \( {@A0@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
